    {
      "name": "priority_numeric",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Numeric extraction of the existing priority field enables grouping/correlation with resolution time, a plausible driver. Slightly redundant with the original priority column but adds modeling convenience; well grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "category_mismatch",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A flag for whether the short_description conflicts with the assigned category could plausibly relate to slower resolution (misrouting). However, groundedness is uncertain: judging a 'mismatch' requires a subjective mapping, and sample rows (e.g. 'Email system not working' flagged 1 without visible category) make the derivation hard to verify."
    },
    {
      "name": "opened_hour",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Hour of day opened is a reasonable axis (off-hours tickets may resolve slower). Grounded in opened_at. Minor concern: sample rows show opened_hour values that don't obviously match the shown timestamps (only sys_updated_on/closed_at shown), but opened_at exists in the table so derivation is plausible."
    },
    {
      "name": "opened_day_of_week",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.72,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Day-of-week gives a genuine grouping axis for resolution-time differences (weekday vs weekend staffing). Derivable from opened_at and consistent with is_weekend in samples."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_weekend",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.5,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly relevant to resolution delays, but largely redundant with opened_day_of_week (a restatement/derivative). Well grounded and consistent with the day-of-week values in samples."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
  "source_groundedness": 0.81,
  "rationale": "The added columns provide the core outcome variable (resolution_hours) plus several plausible explanatory axes (priority, timing, category mismatch) that directly serve the 'why do some incidents take longer' query. Most are well grounded in existing timestamp/priority fields. Weaknesses: is_weekend is largely a derivative of opened_day_of_week, and category_mismatch relies on a subjective derivation that is hard to verify from the samples. No clear hallucinations observed."
